          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How often do they recheck it?",
          "answer": "The conversation is about your thyroid, so I'm assuming you mean the thyroid blood test (TSH, the thyroid-stimulating hormone level).\n\nAccording to the *Hypothyroidism: which test comes first, and the monitoring interval after a change* guideline, TSH is rechecked **six to eight weeks after starting thyroid medication or after any dose change**. The guideline says this wait is needed because the hormone takes that long to settle at its new level. The same guideline says an abnormal result is usually repeated after several weeks before long-term treatment begins. The passages I retrieved did not give a routine recheck interval for someone whose dose is stable, so I can't tell you that from these sources.\n\nYour treating clinician sets your actual schedule, so ask them when your next test is due.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
